{"title":"Career Roadmap · Medical Product Designer","role":"Medical Product Designer","summary":"A Medical Product Designer designs physical products and systems used in healthcare environments by patients, doctors, nurses, technicians and caregivers.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Healthcare / Medical Product Design"},"about":[{"label":"Career","text":"Medical Product Designer"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Medical Product Designer designs physical products and systems used in healthcare environments by patients, doctors, nurses, technicians and caregivers."},{"type":"h","text":"The field combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial/product design"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Healthcare workflows"},{"text":"Medical technology"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Usability engineering"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Safety and regulatory awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Typical products include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diagnostic devices"},{"text":"Patient-monitoring equipment"},{"text":"Surgical instruments"},{"text":"Rehabilitation devices"},{"text":"Mobility aids"},{"text":"Hospital equipment"},{"text":"Wearable medical devices"},{"text":"Home-healthcare products"},{"text":"Medication-delivery products"},{"text":"Assistive technologies"},{"text":"Medical packaging"},{"text":"Healthcare furniture and equipment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The designer's responsibility is not simply to make a medical device attractive. The product must be usable, safe, understandable, accessible and appropriate for its clinical context."}]},{"heading":"Typical Education Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Healthcare/Medical Product Design","Human Factors + Medical Product Development","Healthcare Design Internship","Junior Medical/Industrial Designer","Medical Product Designer","Senior Designer","Design Lead / Healthcare Innovation Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"A strong alternative route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Industrial Design","Healthcare Specialisation","Medical Device Design"]}]},{"heading":"Career Development Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Horizon","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design fundamentals, observation, human-centred design"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Healthcare research, ergonomics, product development"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Medical devices, prototyping, usability and engineering"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Industry project, portfolio, internship"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Junior Medical/Product Designer"}],[{"text":"3–6 Years"},{"text":"Medical Product Designer"}],[{"text":"6–10 Years"},{"text":"Senior Designer / Design Specialist"}],[{"text":"10+ Years"},{"text":"Design Lead / Healthcare Innovation Lead / Design Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Design Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build strong general design capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design fundamentals"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Form development"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Model making"},{"text":"Design history"},{"text":"Design research"},{"text":"Design thinking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Begin human-centred design"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"User journeys"},{"text":"Personas"},{"text":"Contextual research"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Inclusive design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For healthcare design, start observing the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient needs","Clinician needs","Caregiver needs","Hospital/organisation needs"]},{"type":"p","text":"These stakeholders may have conflicting requirements."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Healthcare Product Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Move into healthcare-specific problems."},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare environments"},{"text":"Medical workflows"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Infection-control considerations"},{"text":"Medical materials"},{"text":"Product-service systems"},{"text":"Healthcare UX"},{"text":"Basic anatomy"},{"text":"Basic physiology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design exercises"},{"type":"h","text":"Create concepts for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient mobility"},{"text":"Medication organisation"},{"text":"Elder-care products"},{"text":"Rehabilitation"},{"text":"Home healthcare"},{"text":"Hospital equipment"},{"text":"Diagnostic interfaces"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop capability in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SolidWorks/Fusion 360"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 Portfolio Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Home Medication Management System\""},{"type":"p","text":"Design a product for people who manage multiple medications."},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medication routines"},{"text":"Common user difficulties"},{"text":"Caregiver requirements"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Error possibilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical product"},{"text":"User interface"},{"text":"Medication organisation"},{"text":"Alerts/feedback"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Instructions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Prototype"},{"type":"h","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical prototype"},{"text":"CAD model"},{"text":"UI prototype"},{"text":"User-testing scenario"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Problem","Design requirements","Ideation","Prototype","Testing","Iteration"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Medical Product Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Move toward professional medical-device design."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Usability engineering"},{"text":"Risk-aware design"},{"text":"Medical device workflows"},{"text":"Product architecture"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Electronics awareness"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Embedded systems awareness"},{"text":"Healthcare data interfaces"},{"text":"Design validation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Medical device categories"},{"type":"h","text":"Study products such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient monitors"},{"text":"Diagnostic devices"},{"text":"Infusion systems"},{"text":"Surgical instruments"},{"text":"Rehabilitation equipment"},{"text":"Prosthetic devices"},{"text":"Orthotic devices"},{"text":"Wearables"},{"text":"Home-health devices"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A designer should understand the product's clinical use case without attempting to replace the expertise of doctors, biomedical engineers or regulatory professionals."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Industry Readiness"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should produce a complete medical-product design case study."},{"type":"h","text":"Major Graduation Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Home-Based Remote Patient Monitoring Device\""},{"type":"p","text":"Design a product ecosystem for remote monitoring."},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User requirements"},{"text":"Patient journey"},{"text":"Caregiver workflow"},{"text":"Clinical workflow"},{"text":"Existing products"},{"text":"Accessibility needs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product"},{"type":"h","text":"Design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical device"},{"text":"Sensor interface"},{"text":"Patient interaction"},{"text":"Display/UI"},{"text":"Charging system"},{"text":"Packaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mobile/dashboard concept"},{"text":"Alerts"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Accessibility features"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"Prototype"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Ergonomic evaluation"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Manufacturing considerations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The portfolio should clearly distinguish design concepts from clinically validated medical devices."}]},{"heading":"Medical Product Design Specialisations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Medical Device Designer"},{"text":"General medical devices"}],[{"text":"Diagnostic Product Designer"},{"text":"Diagnostic equipment"}],[{"text":"Surgical Product Designer"},{"text":"Surgical tools/equipment"}],[{"text":"Rehabilitation Product Designer"},{"text":"Recovery and therapy products"}],[{"text":"Assistive Technology Designer"},{"text":"Accessibility and independence"}],[{"text":"Prosthetic Product Designer"},{"text":"Prosthetic systems"}],[{"text":"Orthotic Product Designer"},{"text":"Orthotic devices"}],[{"text":"Wearable Medical Product Designer"},{"text":"Health-monitoring wearables"}],[{"text":"Home Healthcare Designer"},{"text":"At-home medical products"}],[{"text":"Hospital Equipment Designer"},{"text":"Clinical equipment"}],[{"text":"Patient Monitoring Designer"},{"text":"Monitoring systems"}],[{"text":"Healthcare UX Designer"},{"text":"Digital healthcare interfaces"}],[{"text":"Medical HMI Designer"},{"text":"Device interfaces"}],[{"text":"Healthcare Packaging Designer"},{"text":"Medical packaging"}],[{"text":"Human Factors Designer"},{"text":"Usability and safety"}],[{"text":"Healthcare Innovation Designer"},{"text":"New healthcare solutions"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internship Targets","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Target internships with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical-device companies"},{"text":"Healthcare startups"},{"text":"Hospital innovation teams"},{"text":"Biomedical product companies"},{"text":"Rehabilitation companies"},{"text":"Assistive-technology companies"},{"text":"Industrial design consultancies"},{"text":"Healthcare UX teams"},{"text":"Medical equipment manufacturers"},{"text":"Digital-health companies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical Product Design Intern"},{"text":"Industrial Design Intern"},{"text":"Healthcare Design Intern"},{"text":"Human Factors Intern"},{"text":"Medical Device UX Intern"},{"text":"Product Development Intern"},{"text":"Healthcare Innovation Intern"},{"text":"Assistive Technology Design Intern"},{"text":"CAD/Product Design Intern"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"\"Patient Mobility & Rehabilitation Device\""},{"type":"p","text":"Design an assistive product for post-injury rehabilitation."},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient needs"},{"text":"Physiotherapy workflow"},{"text":"Caregiver requirements"},{"text":"Mobility limitations"},{"text":"Existing products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ergonomic form"},{"text":"Adjustable components"},{"text":"Feedback mechanism"},{"text":"Safety features"},{"text":"Storage/transportation solution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Prototype"},{"type":"h","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"3D-printed prototype"},{"text":"Physical mock-up"},{"text":"User-testing protocol"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Evaluation"},{"type":"h","text":"Test:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ease of use"},{"text":"Comfort"},{"text":"Adjustability"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Cleaning"},{"text":"Assembly"},{"text":"Storage"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This provides a strong human-centred healthcare case study."}]},{"heading":"Human Factors & Usability","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most important areas for a medical product designer."},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human error"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Visibility"},{"text":"Affordances"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Error prevention"},{"text":"Learnability"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Physical ergonomics"},{"text":"Interaction consistency"}]},{"type":"h","text":"A medical product may be used under:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stress"},{"text":"Fatigue"},{"text":"Time pressure"},{"text":"Poor lighting"},{"text":"Emergency conditions"},{"text":"Reduced mobility"},{"text":"Limited technical knowledge"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, the interface and physical interaction must minimise avoidable errors."}]},{"heading":"Healthcare & Clinical Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A designer does not need to become a doctor, but should develop healthcare literacy."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn basic concepts in"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Pathology fundamentals"},{"text":"Clinical workflows"},{"text":"Patient journeys"},{"text":"Hospital environments"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Infection-control principles"},{"text":"Healthcare accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Work with specialists"},{"type":"p","text":"Professional projects commonly require collaboration with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Doctors"},{"text":"Nurses"},{"text":"Biomedical engineers"},{"text":"Physiotherapists"},{"text":"Researchers"},{"text":"Human-factors specialists"},{"text":"Regulatory teams"},{"text":"Manufacturing engineers"}]}]},{"heading":"Safety & Regulatory Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Medical products have significantly higher safety and compliance requirements than ordinary consumer products."},{"type":"p","text":"Students should develop working awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical-device classification"},{"text":"Risk management"},{"text":"Usability engineering"},{"text":"Design verification"},{"text":"Design validation"},{"text":"Traceability"},{"text":"Labelling"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Quality systems"},{"text":"Clinical evaluation concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the target market and product, relevant frameworks and standards may include ISO 13485, ISO 14971 and IEC 62366, among others."},{"type":"p","text":"A student should treat these as professional regulatory frameworks to learn and work within, not as something a design portfolio can claim to satisfy by itself."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Useful learning areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial design"},{"text":"Healthcare design"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Design research"},{"text":"Service design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SolidWorks"},{"text":"Fusion 360"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"Rapid prototyping"},{"text":"3D printing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Medical-device development"},{"text":"Healthcare systems"},{"text":"Usability engineering"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Healthcare UX"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Basic electronics"},{"text":"IoT"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, a strong medical-product portfolio and real user research are generally more valuable than collecting unrelated certificates."}]},{"heading":"Jobs After Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Potential entry-level roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Junior Medical Product Designer"},{"text":"Medical Device Designer"},{"text":"Industrial Designer"},{"text":"Healthcare Product Designer"},{"text":"Human Factors Designer"},{"text":"Healthcare UX Designer"},{"text":"Medical Device UX Designer"},{"text":"Assistive Technology Designer"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Product Designer"},{"text":"Healthcare Innovation Designer"},{"text":"Product Development Designer"},{"text":"Medical Equipment Designer"}]}]},{"heading":"Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design questions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why medical product design?"},{"text":"How is medical-product design different from consumer-product design?"},{"text":"How would you design for elderly users?"},{"text":"How do you conduct healthcare user research?"},{"text":"How do you identify usability risks?"},{"text":"How do you balance clinical requirements and user experience?"},{"text":"How would you design for a stressful environment?"},{"text":"How do accessibility requirements affect your design?"},{"text":"How do you validate a product concept?"},{"text":"Explain your strongest healthcare design project."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical questions"},{"type":"h","text":"Prepare for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is human factors engineering?"},{"text":"What is usability engineering?"},{"text":"What is risk-aware design?"},{"text":"What is design verification?"},{"text":"What is design validation?"},{"text":"Why is ergonomics important in medical devices?"},{"text":"What role does prototyping play?"},{"text":"How does manufacturing influence product design?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Industrial/Product Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Broadens product-development capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Medical/Healthcare Design"},{"type":"p","text":"For deeper healthcare specialisation."},{"type":"h","text":"Human Factors / Ergonomics"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong option for medical-device usability."},{"type":"h","text":"Interaction / UX Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical interfaces"},{"text":"Healthcare applications"},{"text":"Connected devices"},{"text":"Digital health"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Biomedical Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible for students willing to build substantially stronger engineering and scientific foundations."},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Innovation"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful for students interested in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare systems"},{"text":"Service innovation"},{"text":"Product strategy"},{"text":"Entrepreneurship"}]}]},{"heading":"High-Value Specialist Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Medical Devices"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Industrial Design","Human Factors","Medical Device Design","Medical Product Designer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — Rehabilitation"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Ergonomics","Rehabilitation","Assistive Technology","Rehabilitation Product Designer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Medical UX"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","UX","Human Factors","Medical HMI","Healthcare UX Designer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — Wearables"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Wearable Design","Sensors/IoT","Health Monitoring","Medical Wearable Designer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route E — Surgical Products"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Product Design","Clinical Workflow","Surgical Instruments","Surgical Product Designer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route F — Healthcare Innovation"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Healthcare Research","Service/Product Design","Healthcare Innovation","Design Strategist"]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Requirements","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build 5–7 substantial case studies."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1"},{"type":"h","text":"Home medication management"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2"},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation device"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical diagnostic product"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4"},{"type":"h","text":"Assistive technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare wearable"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital equipment"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 7"},{"type":"h","text":"Major medical-product graduation project"},{"type":"h","text":"Each case study should demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Context","Users","Research","Clinical/workflow understanding","Requirements","Ideation","Prototype","Testing","Iteration","Final concept"]}]},{"heading":"Professional Medical Product Design Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Problem"},{"type":"h","text":"Stakeholder Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical/Contextual Research"},{"type":"h","text":"User Requirements"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Requirements"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk & Usability Considerations"},{"type":"h","text":"Ideation"},{"type":"h","text":"Concept Development"},{"type":"h","text":"CAD / Prototyping"},{"type":"h","text":"Usability Testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Iteration"},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering Collaboration"},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Verification/Validation Processes"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory & Quality Processes"},{"type":"h","text":"Production"}]},{"heading":"AI in Medical Product Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"AI can support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare research synthesis"},{"text":"Design ideation"},{"text":"Generative product concepts"},{"text":"User journey analysis"},{"text":"Accessibility exploration"},{"text":"CAD assistance"},{"text":"Rapid visualisation"},{"text":"Simulation support"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Usability analysis"},{"text":"Personalised healthcare-product concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI-generated medical-product concepts require much stronger human review than ordinary consumer products."},{"type":"h","text":"Designers must consider:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Safety","clinical context","human factors","privacy","reliability","manufacturability","regulatory requirements."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Future of Medical Product Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Major growth areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Home healthcare"},{"text":"Remote patient monitoring"},{"text":"Medical wearables"},{"text":"Rehabilitation technology"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"AI-enabled diagnostics"},{"text":"Connected medical devices"},{"text":"Digital therapeutics"},{"text":"Personalised healthcare"},{"text":"Robotic medical systems"},{"text":"Smart prosthetics"},{"text":"3D-printed medical products"},{"text":"Elder-care technology"},{"text":"Accessible healthcare products"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The field is increasingly moving toward connected physical-digital healthcare ecosystems rather than isolated devices."}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Career Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Medical-product design is likely to evolve from:"},{"type":"h","text":"Physical medical devices"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Connected devices"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Wearable healthcare"},{"type":"h","text":"→ AI-assisted healthcare products"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Personalised medical devices"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Adaptive rehabilitation systems"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Human-AI healthcare interfaces"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Integrated physical + digital healthcare ecosystems"},{"type":"p","text":"Designers who understand industrial design + human factors + healthcare + digital technology will have particularly strong opportunities."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad Opportunities","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students can explore healthcare and industrial-design ecosystems in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"United States"},{"text":"United Kingdom"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Italy"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Japan"},{"text":"South Korea"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Potential postgraduate areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical Design"},{"text":"Healthcare Design"},{"text":"Industrial Design"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Healthcare Innovation"},{"text":"Biomedical Design"},{"text":"Interaction Design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For specialised programmes, a strong portfolio demonstrating research, prototyping and human-centred design is important."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Medical/Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Design support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3–5 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complete product development"},{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Engineering collaboration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Medical Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complex medical products"},{"text":"Design strategy"},{"text":"Mentoring"},{"text":"Cross-functional leadership"}]},{"type":"h","text":"8–12 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Lead / Healthcare Innovation Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product portfolio"},{"text":"Design systems"},{"text":"Innovation strategy"},{"text":"Team leadership"}]},{"type":"h","text":"12+ Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Director / Healthcare Design Strategist / Innovation Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare product strategy"},{"text":"Design organisation"},{"text":"Innovation"},{"text":"Long-term product vision"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial design"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Healthcare design"},{"text":"Design research"},{"text":"Visual communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic anatomy"},{"text":"Basic physiology"},{"text":"Clinical workflows"},{"text":"Patient journeys"},{"text":"Healthcare accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human Factors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Error prevention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"3D modelling"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Basic electronics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Healthcare UX"},{"text":"HMI"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Connected-device concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Design documentation"},{"text":"Engineering collaboration"},{"text":"Regulatory awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted design"},{"text":"Medical wearables"},{"text":"IoT"},{"text":"Digital health"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Generative design"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"h","text":"Design fundamentals + human-centred design"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"flow","items":["Healthcare research","ergonomics","product development"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"flow","items":["Medical devices","prototyping","usability","engineering"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4"},{"type":"flow","items":["Major healthcare product","industry internship","portfolio"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Graduation"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Medical/Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"3–6 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Product Designer / Human Factors Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"6–10 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Designer / Design Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"10+ Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Innovation Lead / Design Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A highly competitive B.Des Medical Product Designer graduate should demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Strong industrial-design fundamentals","healthcare user research","ergonomics and human-factors knowledge","CAD/3D modelling","physical prototyping","usability testing","healthcare workflow understanding","medical-device regulatory awareness","5–7 strong healthcare case studies","industry internship experience","digital/AI healthcare knowledge."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key differentiator is the ability to design for real clinical and patient contexts, rather than simply making a medical device look modern. A strong designer can connect patient needs, clinical workflow, usability, safety, engineering constraints and manufacturing into one coherent product."}]}]}